          "output_json": {
            "finding": "POST /orders returned HTTP 500 (39.6 5xx/2m vs 179.6 200s) with `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'strip'` on release fault-release-b842fdd053bc49e9 (source_sha 5b51e9fa...). The known-good→incident diff showed apps/order_api/pricing.py dropped the `(coupon or '')` fallback so the line became `coupon.strip().upper()`. Because `Order.coupon` is optional and defaults to None in app.py, any order created without a coupon passed None into total_cents() and crashed before reaching the 422 handler, producing a 500 instead of a normal non-discounted order. Repair restored the existing known-good guard as a one-line change with no behavioral change for valid, blank, or invalid coupons. Added new regression test tests/order/test_pricing_optional_coupon.py covering None, empty, whitespace-only, case/padding normalization, and unknown-coupon rejection. run_tests passed all 6 cases, and the independent HTTP oracle confirmed coupon=null now returns total_cents=20000 with persisted and idempotent rows. PR opened, not merged or deployed.",
